WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.147 --> 00:00:02.730
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.630
- Does that person know Jesus?

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.130
Where is he the way to Jesus?

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.230
Is he also going to heaven?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.163
Because I see Christ in every
human being, I'd say no.

00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:21.746
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.768
- [Interviewer] Christianity
is the only path to salvation.

00:00:30.768 --> 00:00:31.601
3, 2, 1.

00:00:36.994 --> 00:00:37.827
- Yeah, I would say agree

00:00:37.827 --> 00:00:42.420
because I believe that
Jesus is God and his life,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.290
his death, his resurrection
is the great redemption

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.940
that God had for the world.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.920
- If you really think
about it, if you believe

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.640
Jesus is not the only way,
you're calling God an idiot,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.700
'cause you think he's gonna
say one day, "Oh, shoot.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.310
You could go to Heaven
by being a good person."

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.280
Or, "And I spent all this energy and time

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.200
to sacrifice my own son,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.600
why didn't somebody tell
me there was another way?"

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.610
I mean, if there was another way,

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.290
Jesus would not have gone to the cross.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.890
- Do you think it may
be just a tad harmful

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.840
to say that were calling God an idiot

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.410
for those that maybe haven't
come to that conclusion yet,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.020
or maybe people that are
wrestling through that?

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.190
'Cause I mean, think about it like this.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:27.360
If I grew up, or if we
grew up in an Islamic,

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.770
predominantly Islamic territory,
could we confidently say

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.470
that we would still be
Christian in those environments?

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:38.640
I love your passion. I
just fear we as Christians

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.760
have caused so much hurt by just how we've

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.060
communicated things and just
in not giving people room

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.363
to be messy in their beliefs
and messy in where they are.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:53.227
- [Interviewer] I support the
LGBTQ+ community. 3, 2, 1.

00:01:58.887 --> 00:02:01.770
- I'm just curious to
see what support means.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.480
I feel like a lot of Christians,

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.220
at least that I've been friends with,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.520
I mean even myself at
one point would be afraid

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.940
of saying that I support
the LGBT community.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.790
- I know that we're just
called to love our neighbors.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.800
And if my neighbor's LGBTQ,

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.750
there's no reason why I can't love them.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.620
Especially where we live,
to not invite people

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.410
of that community into our
churches, into our lives,

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.670
into whatever we have going on,

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.830
would be just like a
big loss for the church,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.230
because especially where
we're at in the country,

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.850
that's a very big demographic.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.060
And so I think missing
out on that would just be

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.350
a shame for the church.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.183
- See, that's the thing.

00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:41.010
I agree with everything that
you've said, because I know

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.890
that God loves them and
they are a minority group

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.930
that's been persecuted wrongfully.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.080
And I believe no one
should be shamed or beat up

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.630
based on their sexual orientation,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:55.290
but the thing is what people
do with their sex life

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.600
in their own bedrooms
is none of my business.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:58.950
I'm not gonna say anything about that.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.390
I don't really care what they do.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:04.230
But when they come to my area
and they tell me that my God

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.840
thinks all that is okay,
that's when I have a problem.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.550
But in terms of supporting,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.860
their view of God is what I don't support.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.040
- I would also say, though,
that that's a big generalization

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.470
just like people generalize
Christians and say

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:18.480
Christians hate gay people.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.100
There's a lot of gay people who literally

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.460
don't give two craps what
Christians believe, you know?

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.890
It's kind of the same way, as
much as we wanna love people

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.110
and we have experienced the love of Jesus

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.570
and we want other people
to experience that,

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.220
I'm not gonna love someone with an agenda.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.120
I'm not gonna love them

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.160
with the hope that one
day they'll convert.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:35.993
I'm gonna love them.

00:03:35.993 --> 00:03:38.310
- Would you say that being gay is a sin?

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.143
- No.

00:03:39.143 --> 00:03:41.220
What do you think would
classify being a part

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.990
of the LGBT community?

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.100
- Homosexual activity.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.470
- Because I would consider, I'm gay,

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:51.120
but for some Christians just phrasing that

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.120
is horrifying, because they
believe that being gay is a sin.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.980
Personally, I think that there's cultural

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:02.940
and societal attachments to
the concept of being gay.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.700
But if you just take it down
to the textbook, I mean,

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.630
being gay is simply
attraction to the same sex.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:12.330
- Some of you are saying
that you would advocate

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.600
for celibacy for the LGBTQ community

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.090
if they want to be Christian or not?

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.980
- I think most Christians
are on the same page

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.610
of being gay is not a sin,
but it's more so what you do

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.290
with the fact that you are gay.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.630
Kind of delineates what's
sin and what's not.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.720
- And I would even say,
it's not my place to decide

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.840
if it's right for a gay person
to choose to be celibate.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.850
If someone wants to put something
in their mouth, they can.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.490
I don't think I should have
any opinion in that matter,

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.410
'cause it's not my life,
it's not my sex life.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.243
You know what I mean?

00:04:41.243 --> 00:04:42.120
'Cause we don't have opinions

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.280
on heterosexual relationships.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.980
I mean, aside from sex before marriage,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.380
but it's like we're not asking
people what they're doing

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.213
in their free time.

00:04:50.213 --> 00:04:51.046
You know what I mean?

00:04:51.046 --> 00:04:53.010
- I think a question we
have to ask as evangelicals

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:58.010
is why the LGBTQ community
doesn't feel safe in our spaces?

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:03.210
And I think that is a question
that should be primary,

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.450
if we really do love and
accept people as made

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.210
in the image of God, why
don't they feel safe,

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.640
and why do they feel like
they have to leave our spaces?

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.390
And I've had so many gay
friends leave the church,

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.580
leave Christianity,

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.830
so many people part of
this LGBTQ community.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.190
And so that is the
question that I lead with

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.610
in how I talk about and think about

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.013
how we love and care
for the LGBTQ community.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.730
- [Interviewer] Evangelicals
are misunderstood

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.287
or mischaracterized by the media.

00:05:35.287 --> 00:05:36.120
3, 2, 1.

00:05:46.471 --> 00:05:49.221
(Angel whimpers)

00:05:52.097 --> 00:05:53.790
- Sorry. Oh, my gosh.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:57.060
Sorry. It's just that is so hard.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:02.060
I do feel like media outlets
sometimes can focus on failures

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.550
in Christian leadership and stuff.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:09.060
In that regard, looking at these examples

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.280
in a way that feels portrayed,

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.350
in a way that feels frustrated,

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.120
then I would go on that side.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.210
- A lot of the times the
negative media that does come

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.860
to the church or Christianity,
is because of one extreme.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.660
Again, that's just a generalization.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.100
If you see one group doing one thing

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.230
that doesn't mean the whole
Body of Christ is doing it.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.720
- If the prompt were Christians,

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.430
I would definitely be on this side.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.350
I think the reason I
would choose this side

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:37.590
for the term 'evangelicals'
is because generally,

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:41.400
vast majority, like 80% of
evangelicals voted for Trump.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.240
I do think a lot of the
news or the coverage

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.960
about who we are and our failures is real.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.020
And it's kind of like the
stark reality of our church.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.020
A lot of the issues that we see,

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:56.340
I think we need to own them.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.500
I think we need to apologize for them.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.270
I think we need repent from them.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.450
And I think we need to show
people who Jesus really is,

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.840
apart from this sort of
conglomerate movement that we have.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.800
And I do think we're more
represented right now.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:14.790
Also, there's so many
evangelicals doing beautiful work

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.080
that represents who Jesus is

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.150
and what the kingdom of
God looks like, absolutely.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.460
But I think we need to own that the media

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.500
isn't covering things
that they're making up,

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.753
they're covering things
that are really happening

00:07:24.753 --> 00:07:26.253
(people cheer)
in the church.

00:07:28.867 --> 00:07:30.192
- Oh, my God.

00:07:30.192 --> 00:07:32.175
(people laugh)
- Yeah.

00:07:32.175 --> 00:07:35.258
(indistinct chatter)

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.190
- [Interviewer] Women should
be allow the leadership roles

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:41.607
in the church.

00:07:41.607 --> 00:07:42.440
3, 2, 1.

00:07:48.148 --> 00:07:49.620
- Well... (chuckles)

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.000
I didn't want to open my mouth

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.160
so I don't get taken out of context.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.840
So I wanna first start off by saying

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.230
I do believe that women
are valuable and crucial

00:07:58.230 --> 00:07:59.970
in the leadership of the church.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:04.350
And God has defined gender
roles for the family.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:08.490
I've had wonderful women
pastors preach at my church.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.890
And so I do believe
women pastors are good.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:14.850
But I believe that the
senior pastor of the church

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.640
is the father of the church family.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.740
And the father is a male.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.530
- I think there's a loose
definition of leadership.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:25.890
And I don't know if we're
referring to specific positions

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:26.850
within the church.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:28.530
But I do feel like even in the Bible

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.810
there's so many instances of females

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.130
expressing like leadership.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:37.130
- As a woman who is
studying to be a pastor,

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.870
I appreciate that you say that

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.340
you think women can be pastors.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:44.700
I do still think there's
harm in over-differentiating.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.220
I think something Jesus
says is, or not Jesus,

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.070
something Paul says is there's
no more male or female.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:54.450
And ultimately I think part of
what Jesus brings is equality

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.073
where there was once difference.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.502
- [Interviewer] The Bible
should be interpreted literally.

00:09:00.502 --> 00:09:01.335
3, 2, 1.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.840
- I think to interpret the Bible literally

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.480
is a very Western Christianity thing.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.790
And so I'm not gonna say
that one person who doesn't

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.280
take the Bible word for word
is in the wrong with that.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.900
- Yeah, I think the Bible is absolutely

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.320
the inspired word of God, and
that we need to understand it.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:28.860
But we need to understand it
in its contexts and its genre,

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.660
and make sure we pay careful attention

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:33.390
to not just put our Western lens on.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.940
And I think that's how
we can treat the Bible

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:36.780
most faithfully.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.500
- I agree with that, that
there are different genres,

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.560
so I don't take every little
thing as literal in the Bible.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.790
I take it as I see it.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.740
- I'd be curious to see your perspective

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:47.940
on some of the psalms.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.220
- Yeah. So as she
mentioned, different genres

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.320
like Revelation, isn't all literal.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.800
But the message where most
of what the Bible says,

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.170
I think should be taken at face value,

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.400
is what I mean by literal.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.200
- There's still some
room for interpretation

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.033
with that, though.

00:10:02.033 --> 00:10:04.200
So it's like how literal
is that? You know?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.190
- Yeah.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:08.490
Especially when your perspective
can be shaped so much

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:10.350
off of cultural and societal upbringing.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:11.183
- [Kayli] Yeah.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:15.486
- [Interviewer] I support the
overturning of Roe V Wade.

00:10:15.486 --> 00:10:16.319
3, 2, 1.

00:10:20.304 --> 00:10:23.387
(indistinct chatter)

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:30.060
- I think you can absolutely
believe in the sanctity of life

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.550
and the sacredness of choice.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:35.580
And when it comes to medical
decisions, I don't see why

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.410
anyone else should have a say.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:40.170
There are no other ways
that the government

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.600
is regulating bodily decisions.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.090
I feel like it's just
making abortion unsafe.

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:48.450
It's making it much
more difficult for women

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.570
in low income communities
to get out of their cycles.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:54.270
And so I think it's just gonna
do a lot more harm than good.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.430
And they're coming for
things beyond abortion.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:57.870
They're gonna start
coming for birth control.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:00.150
They're gonna start
coming for contraception.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.650
They've already said that these things are

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.030
they're gonna start working towards,

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:06.030
and this is just kind of
like the first step of it.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:09.090
- I am actually pro-life, but
I think we should have done

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:11.340
a lot of groundwork in investing more

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:12.510
in the foster care system,

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.430
investing more in women's healthcare,

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:19.430
investing more in education and
all these different spheres.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:23.010
Anybody who was pro-life,
I think we also need to be

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.990
the ones to also step up and invest more

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.870
in women and children.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.520
We need to be putting our
money where our mouth is,

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.350
and putting our time and our resources.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:32.790
- I totally agree with all that.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.430
And as you mentioned, I
think there's a lot of issues

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.530
around abortion and Roe V Wade.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:40.140
But I don't really see this
as an evangelical issue

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:43.620
or even a religious issue,
I see it as moral issue.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.110
When is it okay to kill a baby?

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.420
And overturning Roe V Wade
is saying you shouldn't

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.460
- I don't even think any pro-choice person

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.930
is wanting to kill babies.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:56.520
I think that is a very
harsh use of language.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.400
Because also 70% of women
who have had abortions

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.540
identify as Christian.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.340
And so in using language like that,

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.410
especially when it's
coming from the pulpit

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.810
or whatever, it is that is so harmful

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.850
because women in your
churches, in your pews,

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:11.340
in your small groups, and
whatever, someone there

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:14.880
has probably had to be
faced with that decision.

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.630
And so when we, as the church
are using such harsh language,

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.550
it's kind of putting a wall,
it's putting a barrier,

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.900
and it's pushing people away.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.480
- I also do think that there is something

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.800
somewhat disheartening about
how this looks right now,

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:30.480
that all males are on this side

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.310
and all females are on that side.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.780
Personally, I don't necessarily agree

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.580
with using the language of killing babies

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.790
because that's like the darkest day

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:42.390
in some of these ladies'
lives, the darkest day.

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:45.570
- And if I could, I
would go more that way,

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.480
because you are right,
there are a lot of issues,

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.490
and personally, I
haven't experienced them.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.080
But I think the question is still

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.823
when is it okay to kill a baby?

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:59.990
- I just don't feel like as
a guy, I could say much to--

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.986
I don't know, maybe-- I don't
know what I'm doing right now.

00:13:03.986 --> 00:13:05.130
(people laugh)

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:07.140
- You're right. If it was about opinions,

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.940
which basketball team is better.

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:12.210
I think opinions, whatever,
everybody's opinion is the same.

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:14.040
But because as evangelicals,

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.160
we stand on what the word
of God is saying to us.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:19.410
We can stand on whether
something is right or wrong,

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:20.820
or we could say that

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.320
we could be wrong about
that, you're right.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.960
- I think any person who was pro-life,

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:28.260
we need to be putting
ourselves in a situation

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.360
where we are bearing that cost as well.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:33.810
And it's not enough just to
donate some money every month,

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:34.680
right, and support.

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:37.170
I think all of us need to
actually have skin in this game

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:38.247
if we're gonna be pro-life.

00:13:38.247 --> 00:13:40.230
And I think the church
really needs to step up

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.930
and be the ones to
actually go to all those--

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.470
to go to the women
directly, to really put--

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.790
It needs to cost us something.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.310
- I'm excited to see
the church equally fight

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.590
for the sanctity of life at all levels.

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:55.710
And not just in terms of
the mother and the baby,

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:59.490
but in terms of, yeah,
people experiencing all kinds

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:02.190
of quality of life and that yeah,

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:06.210
I feel like talking about the
sanctity of life has become

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:09.870
politicized in terms of how
we care for the immigrant

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:13.440
versus how we care for the
woman having an abortion.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:16.200
And I'd love to see us as
the church be vocal about

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.445
caring about life in general.

00:14:18.445 --> 00:14:20.736
- [Interviewer] I think we
get to wrap up (indistinct).

00:14:20.736 --> 00:14:22.493
(indistinct) a round of applause.

00:14:22.493 --> 00:14:24.993
(people clap)

00:14:28.317 --> 00:14:31.603
- I'm proud to be a citizen of my country.

00:14:31.603 --> 00:14:34.738
♪ Proud to be an American ♪

